nditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative topics for this level", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative topics for this level", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative topics for this level", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Simple Present vs. the Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about actions that are happening now.<br> You use the Simple Present tense to talk about habits, routines and things that are generally true.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I usually walk to work.<br> I often have coffee after lunch.<br> It really hurts.<br> How do I get back?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Today, I'm taking the bus.<br> I'm having tea this afternoon.<br> My foot is throbbing.<br> I am not moving for a while!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals Must and Should", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">must </span> to talk about things that are necessary or that you have an obligation to do.<br><br> You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span>  to give advice. There is no obligation. It is only a suggestion.<br><br>You can also use <span class=\"italic\">should </span> for suggestions and recommendations.<br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You must stop at a red light.<br> I must ask my father before I take his car.<br> You must keep your foot elevated.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You should take a day off.<br> I should try that new restaurant.<br> We should go to bed early tonight.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to throb", "type": "name"}, {"content": "pain with strong regular beat", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hit my thumb, and it's now throbbing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you get medical help.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the part of the foot at the back", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My right heel hurts when I step down. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "pulled and kept together firmly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These shoes are too tight, so I need a bigger size.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to wrap", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cover", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He wrapped my ankle so I could walk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crutch", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a wooden support to help someone walk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I broke my leg. I walk with a crutch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "elevated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a position up off the ground", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The doctor kept my foot elevated so it didn't hurt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reduce", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to bring down the amount or size", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Put ice on your knee to reduce the swelling.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write what you want to tell the doctor about a hiking injury.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain where the pain is and how it feels.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask the doctor for advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask if you need medication.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe an injury to a doctor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express feelings about pain and my general health condition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for medical advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about my injury to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}